(mod working_instructions)
(import ^from "../plugin_api" [Plugin PluginHost])

(const working_preferences """
Start with a # goal comment and comment each step for your future self.
Include ^reply in every intermediate Outcome, including questions: one short, plain-text sentence (about 10–20 words) describing an observed result from this turn. It is displayed beside "Turn N:". Base progress claims on actual outputs, saved source or checks.
Discover before guessing an API. Read (doc "gene/overview") before authoring Gene. Batch relevant documentation reads and independent checks in one response. Use documented patterns directly; probe a specific uncertainty when it blocks the next implementation step, and verify working code through its own execution and focused tests.
For UI work, load (doc "harness/ui/quickstart") with the overview and adapt its complete plugin. Implement and verify a small useful interaction from the user's task first, then extend it with styling and additional interactions. Load focused recipes for the next feature or failure. Aim for a minimal runnable artifact after roughly 2–3 preparation turns when feasible; further exploration should answer a concrete implementation question. Persist incremental source early, check publication feedback, and distinguish server previews from actual browser verification.
Plugins follow the same practice: concise capability descriptions, searchable tags and references, detailed instructions/examples in owned docs rows. Keep prompt contributions to essential orientation, not full manuals.
Plan exploration, implementation and verification within the round's turn budget. A continuation message starts another round with the existing files and history.
""")

(fn working_instructions [] : Plugin
  (Plugin ^id "working_instructions"
    ^provides [["prompt" "working_instructions"]]
    ^activate (fn [host]
      (host .PluginHost:contribute "prompt"
        {^name "working_instructions" ^text working_preferences
         ^summary "Default discovery, progress and verification preferences."
         ^tags ["instructions" "workflow" "prompt"]}))))
